<title>USA: FSA qualifies Lowell, Mass bond deal for insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies Lowell, Mass bond deal for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>FSA said on Thursday that it had qualified a fifth bond deal for insurance slated for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>The issue the company added was Lowell, Mass., $44 million of general obligations.</p>
<p>Earlier, the company had qualified the following four issues:</p>
<p>--Cotati-Rohnert Park, Calif., $9 million of GOs.</p>
<p>--Brockport Central School District, N.Y., $3.130 of bonds.</p>
<p>--Chesterfield County, S.C., $2.4 million of GOs.</p>
<p>--Vernon County, Wis., $1.650 million of GO promissory notes.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
